# .gitattributes — 15AUG2026 v1.1 · Flame (pre-freeze repair: +jsonl, +self)
# Practical: the red-team gate binds SHA-256 to EXACT bytes (harness/redteam.py),
# and the freeze ledger hashes LF-CANONICAL bytes (scenarios/manifest.py::
# canonical_file_bytes — TV-1 stop-ship #1 repair, 15AUG2026). core.autocrlf on
# Windows would rewrite LF→CRLF at checkout; these rules pin the byte
# representation so working trees match Git storage and the canonical hasher.
#
# Philosophical: a review belongs to words in a particular arrangement — down
# to the newline. The newline is part of the witness.

*.json  text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.csv   text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
*.svg   text eol=lf
*.ipynb text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.gitignore     text eol=lf

*.png   binary
